<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21147] ofd: adaptive heat-based OST read cache</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21147</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Problem%2FMotivation"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem / Motivation&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Today, the OSD read cache decides whether to cache read pages using two static, device-wide size thresholds checked on every I/O: &lt;tt&gt;readcache_max_io_mb&lt;/tt&gt; (default 8 MiB on &lt;tt&gt;osd-ldiskfs&lt;/tt&gt;) and &lt;tt&gt;readcache_max_filesize&lt;/tt&gt; (default &lt;tt&gt;totalram / 64&lt;/tt&gt; on &lt;tt&gt;osd-ldiskfs&lt;/tt&gt;, unlimited on &lt;tt&gt;osd-zfs&lt;/tt&gt;). Because there is no memory of past client access, a large shared file read by hundreds of clients is excluded from the OST page cache/ARC once it exceeds &lt;tt&gt;readcache_max_filesize&lt;/tt&gt;, while a small file read by a single client is cached on the OST even though that client already holds the data in its own page cache under a DLM &lt;tt&gt;PR&lt;/tt&gt; lock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Furthermore, &lt;tt&gt;osd-zfs&lt;/tt&gt; currently lacks both the &lt;tt&gt;read_cache_enable&lt;/tt&gt; master switch and the &lt;tt&gt;readcache_max_io_mb&lt;/tt&gt; threshold present on &lt;tt&gt;osd-ldiskfs&lt;/tt&gt;, and &lt;tt&gt;osd_bufs_get()&lt;/tt&gt; does not forward &lt;tt&gt;enum dt_bufs_type&lt;/tt&gt; flags to &lt;tt&gt;osd_bufs_get_read()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="SolutionOverview"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Solution Overview&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add an optional adaptive OST read-cache policy in &lt;tt&gt;ofd&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;obdfilter.*.readcache_adaptive_enable&lt;/tt&gt;, default 0) that tracks recent distinct-client read fan-in per object using time-decaying Bloom filters and passes the caching verdict to the OSD via &lt;tt&gt;dt_bufs_type&lt;/tt&gt; flags. When enabled, this classification replaces static size thresholds on the read path in both &lt;tt&gt;osd-ldiskfs&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;osd-zfs&lt;/tt&gt; (while still honoring the &lt;tt&gt;read_cache_enable&lt;/tt&gt; master switch), and brings &lt;tt&gt;osd-zfs&lt;/tt&gt; to tunable parity by adding &lt;tt&gt;read_cache_enable&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;readcache_max_io_mb&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
